{#-
  Tool-calling chat template for microsoft/Phi-4-mini-instruct (and the mlx-community
  quantizations), whose own template ignores the OpenAI `tools=` argument.

  Derived from vLLM's examples/tool_chat_template_phi4_mini.jinja
  (https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm, Apache-2.0, Copyright contributors to the vLLM
  project). Same prompt text and layout. Changes made in this fork (vllm-mlx):
    * assistant `tool_calls` are rendered in the format the system prompt asks the
      model to produce, `functools[{...}, {...}]`; upstream renders a bare
      `{...}, {...}` that the model was never told to emit, and drops the calls when
      the assistant message also has content;
    * `arguments` that reach the template as a mapping (the server parses the OpenAI
      JSON string) are rendered as JSON, not as a Python dict repr;
    * the OpenAI `tool` role is handled like upstream's `tools` role; a result that is
      not already a JSON object/array is rendered as a JSON string so
      `{"result": ...}` stays valid JSON.
    * the trailing `<|assistant|>` follows `add_generation_prompt` (default: added).
  Use with `--tool-call-parser phi4_mini_json`.
-#}
{%- if messages and messages[0]['role'] == 'system' %}
    {%- set system_message = messages[0]['content']|trim %}
    {%- set messages = messages[1:] %}
{%- else %}
    {%- set system_message = "You are a helpful assistant." %}
{%- endif %}

{%- if messages %}
<|system|>
{{ system_message }}
{%- if tools %}
In addition to plain text responses, you can choose to call one or more of the provided functions.

Use the following rule to decide when to call a function:
  * if the response can be generated from your internal knowledge (e.g., as in the case of queries like "What is the capital of Poland?"), do so
  * if you need external information that can be obtained by calling one or more of the provided functions, generate a function calls

If you decide to call functions:
  * prefix function calls with functools marker (no closing marker required)
  * all function calls should be generated in a single JSON list formatted as functools[{"name": [function name], "arguments": [function arguments as JSON]}, ...]
  * follow the provided JSON schema. Do not hallucinate arguments or values. Do to blindly copy values from the provided samples
  * respect the argument type formatting. E.g., if the type is number and format is float, write value 7 as 7.0
  * make sure you pick the right functions that match the user intent


        {%- for t in tools %}
            {{- t | tojson(indent=4) }}
            {{- "\n\n" }}
        {%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}<|end|>

    {%- for message in messages %}
        {%- if message.role != "system" %}
<|{{ "tools" if message.role == "tool" else message.role }}|>
            {%- if message.role in ["tool", "tools"] and message.content is string %}
                {%- set result = message.content|trim %}
{"result": {{ result if result[:1] in ["{", "["] else result|tojson }}}
            {%- elif message.role in ["tool", "tools"] and message.content %}
{"result": {{ message.content|tojson }}}
            {%- else %}
                {%- if message.content %}
{{ message.content }}
                {%- endif %}
                {%- if message.tool_calls %}
{#- #}functools[
                    {%- for call in message.tool_calls %}
{"name": "{{ call.function.name }}", "arguments": {{ call.function.arguments if call.function.arguments is string else call.function.arguments|tojson }}}
                        {%- if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}
                    {%- endfor %}]
                {%- endif %}
            {%- endif %}<|end|>
        {%- endif %}
    {%- endfor %}
    {%- if add_generation_prompt is not defined or add_generation_prompt %}<|assistant|>{% endif %}

{%- else %}
    {%- if system_message %}
<|system|>

{{ system_message }}<|end|>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- if prompt %}
<|user|>

{{ prompt }}<|end|>
    {%- endif %}<|assistant|>

{%- endif %}
{{ response }}
{%- if response %}<|user|>{% endif %}
